PHP for OpenVMS (vms-php) - news
=================================

8.5.12-vms2 (2026-10)

  SQLite and PDO: the sqlite3, PDO, pdo_sqlite and pdo_mysql extensions,
  with SQLite 3.54.1 from SQLite for OpenVMS (vms-sqlite) built in. Its
  OpenVMS VFS makes one database safe to share between processes and
  accounts (rollback journals; no WAL; no loadable extensions). PHP's
  sqlite3/PDO/pdo_sqlite tests give the same results as on Linux, and a
  phpBB 3.3 board on SQLite passed its checklist and a load run. PHP itself
  (8.5.12) and the other extensions are unchanged from 8.5.12-vms1.

8.5.12-vms1 (2026-10)

  Security update: PHP 8.5.12, which fixes CVE-2026-109618 and
  CVE-2026-109619 (GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w, GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp: remote code
  execution through state corrupted by an out-of-memory or other bailout).
  The VMS patches and the extension set are unchanged.

8.5.11-vms1 (2026-10)

  First kit. PHP 8.5.11 for OpenVMS x86-64, built with VSI clang (LP64):
  - CLI (PHP.EXE) and CGI/FastCGI (PHP_CGI.EXE -b); opcache built in, with
    a file cache;
  - the phpBB extension set (README.VMS section 2), mysqli for MariaDB,
    openssl through VSI's SSL3, Argon2 password hashing, the DNS functions
    through TCP/IP Services;
  - CA certificates for outgoing HTTPS (Mozilla's, via curl.se);
  - runs the phpBB 3.3 board in production behind lighttpd for OpenVMS.
